Return bytes from text connections as unsigned, so a 0xff byte is data
rather than R_EOF where char is signed; the scan target stopped timing
out on inputs containing 0xff.

text_fgetc() (src/main/connections.c) returned (int) of a signed char,
so 0xff became -1 == R_EOF and every reader stopped at the first 0xff:
readLines(textConnection("a\xffb")) gave character(0) and scan() saw
end-of-file inside a quoted string, then again on every subsequent read
(one "EOF within quoted string" warning per remaining field).

The upstream PR also adds a regression test (tests/reg-tests-1e.R),
not carried here.

Found by OSS-Fuzz: testcase 6065703271333888 (libFuzzer_r_scan,
Timeout; 56 KB input, 348 warnings).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #374, filed 2026-10-10 (no Bugzilla
report yet).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/main/connections.c
+++ b/src/main/connections.c
@@ -3593,7 +3593,8 @@
 	return c;
     }
     if(this->cur >= this->nchars) return R_EOF;
-    else return (int) (this->data[this->cur++]);
+    /* as unsigned, or a 0xff byte reads as R_EOF where char is signed */
+    else return (unsigned char) this->data[this->cur++];
 }
 
 static double text_seek(Rconnection con, double where, int origin, int rw)
